      "content": "Companies like Apple and Microsoft argue that their closed ecosystems are necessary for ensuring user safety and maintaining a high level of quality control. They claim that providing unrestricted access to internal components could lead to dangerous malfunctions or compromise proprietary security features. Furthermore, they assert that their repair processes are designed to protect their intellectual property and maintain the integrity of their software experience. These arguments are fundamentally about maintaining their control over the product experience.",
